<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1574" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăgĭtātus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		agito, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a state of motion</i>, <i>a being in motion</i>,
				<i>movement</i>, <i>agitation</i>
			(only ante- and post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 12</span></i>
			Müll. dub. (Müll. reads: ubi id agitatur); <i><span class="en">id. ib.
			6</span></i>, § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">41 Müll.: anima corpori praestat
					agitatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 2, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si agitatu suo aquam moverit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Sat. 7, 8</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentis,</span>”
				<i>activity</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 6, § 42</span></i>
			 Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
